<phrase>
  id: LANG_REBUILD_COVERS
  desc: a row of Settings, before Reset Settings, an action with no value: the covers the computer put on the iPod at a sync are set aside, and the next sync makes every one again. 'Synced' is the covers that come with a sync, not the ones inside the songs' files
  user: core
  <source>
    *: "Rebuild Synced Covers"
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "Refés les caràtules sincronitzades"
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
<phrase>
  id: LANG_HINT_REBUILD_COVERS
  desc: the hint in the band under Settings while Rebuild Synced Covers is selected, in three lines at most: what the user gets from it
  user: core
  <source>
    *: "Your computer makes every cover again at the next sync, with sharp ones for the main menu."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "A la propera sincronització, l'ordinador torna a crear totes les caràtules, nítides per al menú principal."
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
<phrase>
  id: LANG_REBUILD_COVERS_ABOUT
  desc: on the question's screen of Rebuild Synced Covers, wrapped in lines: one sentence, as the hint under the row has said what it is for: until the next sync the synced covers are missing. Finder and Mac are names kept as they are
  user: core
  <source>
    *: "Until the next sync with Finder on a Mac, synced covers are not shown."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "Fins a la propera sincronització amb el Finder en un Mac no es mostren les caràtules sincronitzades."
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
